WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.935
Panchayats are old.

2
00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:05.390
Constitutional protection for them came

3
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.132
only in 1992.

4
00:00:07.468 --> 00:00:10.265
The seventy-third amendment for panchayats

5
00:00:10.265 --> 00:00:12.998
and the seventy-fourth for municipalities

6
00:00:12.998 --> 00:00:14.721
were passed in 1992.

7
00:00:14.721 --> 00:00:17.192
They came into force in

8
00:00:17.192 --> 00:00:20.534
1993. PESA extended panchayats to

9
00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.409
Scheduled Areas in 1996.

10
00:00:23.748 --> 00:00:24.527
Three tiers,

11
00:00:24.527 --> 00:00:26.111
elections every five years,

12
00:00:26.111 --> 00:00:27.444
run by a State Election

13
00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:29.556
Commission. And at least one-third

14
00:00:29.556 --> 00:00:31.174
of seats for women.

15
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.032
The amendments made panchayats mandatory,

16
00:00:34.032 --> 00:00:35.391
but not powerful.

17
00:00:35.391 --> 00:00:37.542
Funds, functions and staff still

18
00:00:37.542 --> 00:00:39.444
depend on the states.

19
00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:41.300
Your turn.

20
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.226
Which Schedule lists panchayat subjects?
